sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  box rgba(21,101,192,0.04) Internal zone
    participant A as Replica A (branch credit-bureau)
    participant B as Replica B (branch fraud-check)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (pre_instance, pre_token)
  end

  par both branches finish within the same millisecond
    A->>DB: SELECT ... FROM pre_instance WHERE tenant_id=? AND id=? FOR UPDATE
    B->>DB: SELECT ... FROM pre_instance WHERE tenant_id=? AND id=? FOR UPDATE (blocks)
  end
  rect rgba(224,242,241,0.8)
    Note over A,DB: TX A holds the instance row lock
    A->>DB: UPDATE token A status=JOINED at join-checks
    A->>DB: COUNT tokens in scope not yet JOINED -> 1 (B still ACTIVE)
    A->>DB: COMMIT (lock released, A does not advance)
  end
  rect rgba(224,242,241,0.8)
    Note over B,DB: TX B gets the lock after A commits
    B->>DB: lock acquired, UPDATE token B status=JOINED
    B->>DB: COUNT tokens in scope not yet JOINED -> 0
    B->>DB: INSERT one ACTIVE token at underwrite, mark A and B COMPLETED, COMMIT
  end
  Note over A,DB: Without the row lock both replicas could count 1 and neither would advance (lost wakeup), or both could count 0 and create two tokens.
